            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court noted that jurisdiction is barred in Speech or Debate Clause cases when the case is predicated on a legislative act, when adjudication would require questioning a legislative act, or when a member would be forced to defend a legislative act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether the Court owes any special respect to Congress concerning the Speech or Debate Clause."
      }
    ],
