  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg: Do you think we owe any special measure of respect to the Congress concerning the Speech or Debate Clause?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer: What's wrong with this?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy: Can you give me examples of cases where that Act applies?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy: Can you give me instances in which employees of an office of a Senator are covered by these obligations and cannot invoke the Speech or Debate Clause?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito: If this statute was set up so that the defendant here was the Senate, as opposed to the office of a Senator, would you still say that this suit couldn't go forward?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter: Well why doesn't it matter who the defendant is?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens: And how do we do it? I mean, you've said -- I don't want to go too far with a metaphor, but you spoke a moment ago of there being sort of a hole or a space in the legislative sphere when somebody is fired."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia: Why isn't it a waiver of sovereign immunity when you set up a suit that envisions a suit which will be paid off by the Senate? Why isn't that a waiver of sovereign immunity?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens: What if his dissent \u2013 or defense, rather, to the charge is that he was very inefficient in giving me help in legislative hearings and so forth, or words of that kind which might be arguably a legislative act, and that Speech or Debate Clause forbids inquiry into the quality of his performing those duties?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy: What's the test for intruding? If it would chill his exercise of the function in future cases, or if it requires him to talk about legislative decisions, or what?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter: Yes, but what if the Senator doesn't want to put it in? I mean, what if he does not want to waive the privilege? Is his only choice in effect to sit moot and lose the case?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy: Could the Senate direct you to pay this judgment?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "47f898af6e147194b356ffd95201e8f1c5232cb92f077f4a2de84f26f9d6a900",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-47f898af6e14-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy: Could it, if it chose?"
      }
    ],
